  "summary": "Malicious code in fontus (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (bb5b8b4484126f787f9917d91b6815927146a308f64bfb852c57f5d60bf4bfbb)\nAnalysis of fontus 0.0.3 on PyPI did not identify any code paths that exfiltrate installer data, execute attacker-controlled payloads at install or import time, relay caller-supplied data to third-party destinations, distribute live credentials, or establish persistence. No install-time network fetches, no lifecycle shell execution, no reads of credential paths (~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, browser profiles), and no obfuscated or dynamic-exec patterns were observed.\n\n## Source: kam193 (2a8fcff0fd4d827c6f174318ee41ea82eb2667c6d65349a01ca2215aa2f4dd5e)\nThe package most likely performs fingerprinting by exfiltrating basic information and available fonts, with no other functionality.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: PROBABLY_PENTEST - Packages looking like typical pentest packages, but also anything that looks like testing, exploring pre-prepared kits, research & co, with clearly low-harm possibilities.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-fontus\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - The package contains code to exfiltrate basic data from the system, like IP or username. It has a limited risk.\n",
